1
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:12,650
This is Momo.

2
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:14,230
This is a teddy bear.

3
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:15,330
Two eyes.

4
00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:16,520
Soft fur.

5
00:00:16,770 --> 00:00:17,810
One is living.

6
00:00:18,050 --> 00:00:19,090
One is not.

7
00:00:19,182 --> 00:00:19,892
Easy?

8
00:00:20,142 --> 00:00:22,322
Then try the six things in our box.

9
00:00:22,682 --> 00:00:24,372
First, a practice round.

10
00:00:24,602 --> 00:00:25,612
The teddy bear.

11
00:00:25,822 --> 00:00:27,162
Point left for living.

12
00:00:27,382 --> 00:00:28,992
Point right for non-living.

13
00:00:29,242 --> 00:00:29,912
Go!

14
00:00:35,368 --> 00:00:36,318
Locked in!

15
00:00:36,448 --> 00:00:37,518
Non-living.

16
00:00:37,738 --> 00:00:39,078
It never eats.

17
00:00:39,132 --> 00:00:40,002
Non-living!

18
00:00:40,152 --> 00:00:41,472
It's full of cotton.

19
00:00:41,528 --> 00:00:43,508
But it has eyes and fur like me.

20
00:00:43,588 --> 00:00:45,018
Why isn't it living?

21
00:00:45,221 --> 00:00:47,411
The teddy bear is a non-living thing.

22
00:00:47,631 --> 00:00:49,751
Eyes and fur are only how it looks.

23
00:00:49,971 --> 00:00:51,471
We need better clues.

24
00:00:51,981 --> 00:00:53,101
Here is the game.

25
00:00:53,321 --> 00:00:54,881
It's You against the Buddies.

26
00:00:55,091 --> 00:00:56,391
You lock in first.

27
00:00:56,611 --> 00:00:58,831
Then Pip, Basil and Momo answer.

28
00:00:58,953 --> 00:01:01,843
Every time you are right, put up one finger on your other

29
00:01:01,593 --> 00:01:02,273
hand.

30
00:01:02,513 --> 00:01:04,233
No lock-in, no point.

31
00:01:04,453 --> 00:01:06,853
And a cicak is hiding in this video.

32
00:01:07,093 --> 00:01:07,923
Find it!

33
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:14,480
Our six things came from here.

34
00:01:14,690 --> 00:01:17,290
A void deck and a garden in Toa Payoh.

35
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:18,530
Look around.

36
00:01:18,651 --> 00:01:19,361
A mynah.

37
00:01:19,691 --> 00:01:20,471
Ants.

38
00:01:20,671 --> 00:01:21,901
A papaya tree.

39
00:01:22,121 --> 00:01:22,951
A bench.

40
00:01:23,171 --> 00:01:24,131
A bicycle.

41
00:01:24,361 --> 00:01:25,851
A blue recycling bin.

42
00:01:26,081 --> 00:01:27,521
So many different things!

43
00:01:28,108 --> 00:01:32,158
There is a great variety of living and non-living things around us.

44
00:01:32,388 --> 00:01:33,998
This is called diversity.

45
00:01:39,509 --> 00:01:40,289
So many!

46
00:01:40,479 --> 00:01:41,829
How do we keep track?

47
00:01:41,841 --> 00:01:43,261
We put them into groups.

48
00:01:43,501 --> 00:01:44,871
Let's start with six.

49
00:01:45,535 --> 00:01:46,455
Are you ready?

50
00:01:46,875 --> 00:01:47,635
Three!

51
00:01:48,025 --> 00:01:48,665
Two!

52
00:01:49,035 --> 00:01:49,665
One!

53
00:01:50,065 --> 00:01:50,735
Go!

54
00:01:58,118 --> 00:01:58,988
Round one.

55
00:01:59,228 --> 00:02:00,808
The wind-up robot.

56
00:02:01,048 --> 00:02:02,118
Look at it go!

57
00:02:02,328 --> 00:02:03,678
Point left for living.

58
00:02:03,878 --> 00:02:05,518
Point right for non-living.

59
00:02:10,993 --> 00:02:11,943
Locked in!

60
00:02:12,073 --> 00:02:12,773
Living!

61
00:02:12,893 --> 00:02:14,403
It moves, so it's living!

62
00:02:14,452 --> 00:02:15,512
Non-living.

63
00:02:15,782 --> 00:02:17,702
I saw you wind it up, Basil.

64
00:02:17,755 --> 00:02:18,735
Non-living.

65
00:02:18,845 --> 00:02:20,395
Does it ever get hungry?

66
00:02:20,896 --> 00:02:21,676
Watch.

67
00:02:21,896 --> 00:02:23,216
The robot stops.

68
00:02:23,426 --> 00:02:25,276
A spring inside was pushing it.

69
00:02:25,410 --> 00:02:27,880
Nobody winds it up, so it stays still.

70
00:02:28,110 --> 00:02:29,020
All night.

71
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,380
All of day two.

72
00:02:30,808 --> 00:02:33,148
It does not need water, food or air.

73
00:02:33,378 --> 00:02:34,558
It does not grow.

74
00:02:34,768 --> 00:02:37,448
The wind-up robot is a non-living thing.

75
00:02:38,112 --> 00:02:39,152
Pointed right?

76
00:02:39,372 --> 00:02:40,532
One finger up!

77
00:02:40,661 --> 00:02:41,241
Aww.

78
00:02:41,441 --> 00:02:43,041
So moving is not the clue!

79
00:02:43,091 --> 00:02:45,961
Then is a thing that stays still always non-living?

80
00:02:47,345 --> 00:02:48,265
Round two.

81
00:02:48,525 --> 00:02:49,375
Day two.

82
00:02:49,605 --> 00:02:50,675
The green bean.

83
00:02:50,925 --> 00:02:51,975
It is a seed.

84
00:02:52,225 --> 00:02:53,725
It has not moved at all.

85
00:02:53,985 --> 00:02:55,525
Living, or non-living?

86
00:02:55,755 --> 00:02:56,545
Point!

87
00:03:02,012 --> 00:03:02,962
Locked in!

88
00:03:03,092 --> 00:03:04,162
Non-living.

89
00:03:04,382 --> 00:03:06,232
I watched it for one whole day.

90
00:03:06,482 --> 00:03:07,682
It did nothing.

91
00:03:07,730 --> 00:03:08,550
Living!

92
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:10,260
It's green, like a leaf.

93
00:03:10,308 --> 00:03:11,008
Living!

94
00:03:11,128 --> 00:03:12,998
Taugeh grows from green beans.

95
00:03:13,068 --> 00:03:14,198
I eat taugeh!

96
00:03:14,619 --> 00:03:16,359
Three buddies, two answers.

97
00:03:16,579 --> 00:03:18,209
Let's shrink down and watch.

98
00:03:18,429 --> 00:03:19,289
Quietly.

99
00:03:22,664 --> 00:03:23,874
You are tiny now.

100
00:03:24,154 --> 00:03:26,394
The green bean is as big as a bus.

101
00:03:27,806 --> 00:03:28,596
Listen.

102
00:03:32,044 --> 00:03:33,294
The skin splits.

103
00:03:33,574 --> 00:03:34,994
A root pushes out.

104
00:03:37,104 --> 00:03:38,614
Nobody wound it up.

105
00:03:38,904 --> 00:03:40,234
Nobody pushed it.

106
00:03:40,504 --> 00:03:42,274
It is growing by itself.

107
00:03:44,689 --> 00:03:46,629
The green bean is a living thing.

108
00:03:46,869 --> 00:03:48,369
It was living all along.

109
00:03:48,609 --> 00:03:49,689
It took in water.

110
00:03:49,949 --> 00:03:51,389
Then it began to grow.

111
00:03:52,113 --> 00:03:53,193
Pointed left?

112
00:03:53,413 --> 00:03:54,573
One finger up!

113
00:03:54,698 --> 00:03:55,858
I was careful.

114
00:03:56,088 --> 00:03:58,058
But I did not watch long enough.

115
00:03:58,180 --> 00:03:59,900
Momo, living is right.

116
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:02,010
But green is only how it looks.

117
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:04,210
A green pencil is non-living.

118
00:04:04,270 --> 00:04:05,520
No point for me!

119
00:04:05,670 --> 00:04:07,090
So what ARE the clues?

120
00:04:07,964 --> 00:04:10,394
Our box has twenty-five more days to go.

121
00:04:10,614 --> 00:04:12,604
What will be under the cloth on Day thirty?

122
00:04:12,834 --> 00:04:14,314
Find out in Part Two!

123
00:04:15,188 --> 00:04:16,598
Show me your score hand!

124
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:20,510
Now you know!
